& [P6BoundaryImportAndProjectionObligationInventoryV1] is the P6-S01 boundary import and projection obligation inventory
  + [slice_id] is P6-S01
  + [slice_name] is boundary import and projection obligation inventory
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_depth] is deeper_reasoning_required
  + [model_route_reason] is boundary import decides which projection obligations become P6 authority and which remain plan-only support
  + [inventory_result] is projection_obligations_imported_without_projection_materialization
  + [next_gate_result] is P6-S02 may open
  + [projection_fixture_file_creation_authorized] is false
  + [expected_snapshot_creation_authorized] is false
  + [generated_projection_creation_authorized] is false
  + [implementation_code_authorized] is false
  + [dependency_installation_authorized] is false
  + [package_metadata_mutation_authorized] is false
  + [adapter_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [transport_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [UI_implementation_authorized] is false
  + [assignment_authorized] is false
  + [dispatch_authorized] is false
  + [operations_control_authorized] is false
  + [live_machine_control_authorized] is false

  = must: treat this inventory as P6 planning authority only
  = must: preserve accepted P2, P4, P5, P8, FSC4, and IR5 records as boundary inputs, not editable projection drafts
  = must: define P6 gaps as work for P6-S02 through P6-S07, not as immediate permission to create surface code, adapters, UI, fixture files, generated projections, dispatch records, or live effects
  = must: keep source authority, surface projections, surface-local state, generated projections, adapter messages, conversation messages, inbound action proposals, packet candidates, assignments, dispatches, operations decisions, and live-control decisions in distinct authority classes

