& [P6ProjectionSupportVsAuthorityInventory] is the support and authority separation inventory
  + [accepted_authority] is P2 authority kernel completion review
  + [accepted_authority] is P4 planning and packetization completion review
  + [accepted_authority] is P5 runtime planning completion review
  + [accepted_authority] is P8 proof fixture evaluation completion review
  + [accepted_authority] is FSC4 surface boundary map
  + [accepted_support] is IR5 bounded surface projection implementation proof
  + [accepted_support] is Post-P5 readiness surface
  + [plan_only_support] is future projection fixture path set
  + [plan_only_support] is future expected projection snapshots
  + [plan_only_support] is future generated projection ledgers
  + [plan_only_support] is future adapter, transport, UI, IRC, Matrix, web, Codex, terminal, and Langflow implementation choices
  + [not_authorized] is assignment
  + [not_authorized] is dispatch
  + [not_authorized] is operations control
  + [not_authorized] is live machine control

  = must: prevent support records from becoming authority records through projection display
  = must: require a new source-preserved implementation activation before plan_only_support becomes file or code material

& [ForbiddenProjectionMutationList: P6-S01] is the forbidden mutation set for P6-S01
  + [forbidden_mutation] is editing accepted P2, P4, P5, P8, FSC4, or IR5 output files to make projection obligations easier
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating surface state as source authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating graph checkpoint state as source authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating adapter messages or conversation logs as source authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is treating generated projections as proof authority
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating projection fixture files
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating expected snapshots
  + [forbidden_mutation] is creating generated projections
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing UI components
  + [forbidden_mutation] is implementing adapters or transports
  + [forbidden_mutation] is installing Langflow, Matrix, IRC, web, or runtime packages
  + [forbidden_mutation] is authorizing assignment or dispatch
  + [forbidden_mutation] is authorizing operations control or live machine control
  + [forbidden_mutation] is omitting authority_notice from future decision-making projections

  = must: fail P6-S01 review if any forbidden mutation appears in the output

& [P6S01DownstreamGate] is the gate opened by P6-S01
  + [opened_slice] is P6-S02 authority notice freshness and nonpromotion rendering contract
  + [activation_basis] is P6 projection obligation inventory accepted
  + [model_route] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_reason] is authority display determines how humans and agents recognize source authority, stale projections, checkpoint nonauthority, and generated-output limits
  + [completion_review_required] is true

  = must: open P6-S02 only after P6-S01 completion review accepts this boundary import
  = must: keep P6-S03 through P6-S07 gated until their predecessor reviews accept
